      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- degree granting: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- Biology department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- variance of the number of students in each student year: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR\n- standard deviation of the number of students in each student year: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR\n- number of students in each student year: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR\n- Mathematics department: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- subject enrollment number: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\n- number of unique subjects: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n- minimum total units offered: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Biology\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Biology'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, what is the department name and both the variance and standard deviation of the number of students in each student year for that department, considering only departments that are degree granting and are not the Biology department?\n```sql\nWITH student_counts AS ( SELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, msd.STUDENT_YEAR, COUNT(*) AS num_students FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT d JOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY msd ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = msd.DEPARTMENT WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND d.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Biology' GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, msd.STUDENT_YEAR ) SELECT DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(num_students) AS variance_num_students, STDDEV(num_students) AS stddev_num_students FROM student_counts GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n2. For each department and academic year where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the department is Mathematics, provide the number of unique subjects and the minimum total units offered.\n```sql\nSELECT cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR, COUNT(DISTINCT ss.SUBJECT_ID) AS num_unique_subjects, MIN(ss.TOTAL_UNITS) AS min_total_units FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED cso JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON cso.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE AND cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME WHERE cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND ss.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER > 10 GROUP BY cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department that is degree granting and is not the Biology department, what is the department name, the variance of the number of students in each student year for that department, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of students in each student year for that department, and, for the Mathematics department and each academic year where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10, the academic year, the number of unique subjects, and the minimum total units offered? Do not return any rounded answers."
